**New evidence**
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President writes letter to the Prime Minister and Leader of the Opposition to propose suitable person for care-taker PM","publisher":"President of Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-04-04","url":"https://president.gov.pk/president-writes-letter-to-the-prime-minister-and-leader-of-the-opposition-to-propose-suitable-person-for-care-taker-pm","claim":"After the National Assembly was dissolved, the president asked the prime minister and the opposition leader to propose a caretaker prime minister under Article 224A.","locator":"line 25","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct presidential notice with constitutional citation and named officeholders.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Immediate April 2022 transfer procedure inside the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Sharif is named as the opposition leader in the caretaker-selection process; this is inherited transfer context rather than a personal democratic reform.","contrary_evidence":["The notice followed a dissolution crisis and does not by itself show broader democratic strengthening by Sharif."],"lenses":["4B.8","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan: Supreme Court Issues Detailed Judgment on Dismissal of Resolution of No-Confidence Motion Against Then-PM Imran Khan","publisher":"Library of Congress","publication_date":"2022-08-07","url":"https://www.loc.gov/item/global-legal-monitor/2022-08-07/pakistan-supreme-court-issues-detailed-judgment-on-dismissal-of-resolution-of-no-confidence-motion-against-then-pm-imran-khan/","claim":"The Supreme Court held that the deputy speaker's dismissal of the no-confidence motion and the subsequent dissolution of the National Assembly were contrary to the constitution and law and were nullities in law.","locator":"line 39","source_type":"legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official legal summary of the court's detailed judgment, directly tied to the April 2022 constitutional crisis.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Targets the April 2022 transfer crisis and its July 2022 legal resolution.","ruler_attribution":"This is mostly inherited baseline and institutional constraint evidence rather than a direct Shehbaz action, but it defines the transfer environment he entered.","contrary_evidence":["The ruling concerns Khan-era actions, not Sharif's own conduct, though it shaped the inherited democratic baseline."],"lenses":["4B.4","4B.8","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan: Freedom on the Net 2022 Country Report","publisher":"Freedom House","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/pakistan/freedom-net/2022","claim":"Internet freedom remained constricted during the coverage period, with authorities routinely using shutdowns, platform blocking, arrests, and harsh convictions to suppress unwanted online speech, and the report records internet throttling during May 2022 PTI protests.","locator":"overview lines 83-84; key developments lines 92-93; line 170","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent methodology-driven country report with specific examples and citations; some individual throttling reports were contested or denied, but the overall pattern is corroborated elsewhere.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Covers June 2021 to May 2022 and includes the first month of Sharif's premiership.","ruler_attribution":"Partly inherited from the PTI period, but the coverage period overlaps Sharif's first weeks in office and ongoing restrictions under his government; PTA denied some throttling reports.","contrary_evidence":["Some disruptions were infrastructural or denied by PTA, so not every internet problem is political censorship."],"lenses":["4B.6","4B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Federal govt issues instructions to PEMRA for lifting ban on broadcasting Imran's speech","publisher":"Radio Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-11-06","url":"https://www.radio.gov.pk/06-11-2022/federal-govt-issues-instructions-to-pemra-for-lifting-ban-on-broadcasting-imrans-speech","claim":"The federal government instructed PEMRA to lift the ban on broadcasting Imran Khan's speech, and the information minister said the prime minister had directed PEMRA to implement Article 19 of the constitution.","locator":"lines 34-39","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct report of an official instruction from the prime minister, with clear date and named implementing agency.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct November 2022 action inside the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributed to Sharif through the minister's statement; this is a concrete pro-opposition speech decision, though it followed earlier restrictions.","contrary_evidence":["The action came after earlier broadcast restrictions, so it is partial and late rather than a clean baseline reform."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.6","4B.8","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"شفا یوسفزئی کے گھر مسلح افراد کا دھاوا، وزیر اعظم نے واقعے کی رپورٹ طلب کرلی","publisher":"Dawn News Urdu","publication_date":"2022-12-21","url":"https://www.dawnnews.tv/news/1194148","claim":"Sharif strongly condemned the armed intrusion into anchor Shifa Yousafzai's home, asked the Islamabad IG for a report, and directed that the suspects be found and punished under the law.","locator":"lines 65-75","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Local-language outlet quoting the prime minister and police response; strong for the immediate response, weaker for any broader systemic conclusion.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"December 2022, within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Direct PM response to an attack on a journalist; it shows a protective reaction to one incident, not durable system-wide protection.","contrary_evidence":["The underlying incident shows journalists still faced severe insecurity.","A response to one attack does not prove sustained protection of the press."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.6","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan: Immediately release eight people arrested over critical tweets","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-04-13","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2022/04/pakistan-immediately-release-eight-people-arrested-over-critical-tweets/","claim":"The Federal Investigation Agency detained eight people after they published criticism of the state on Twitter, and Amnesty said the arrests were part of a repressive crackdown on free expression online.","locator":"lines 63-64","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct advocacy alert with a dated incident and specific state agency; the attribution is clear even if the broader pattern remains advocacy-framed.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct April 2022 conduct inside the target year.","ruler_attribution":"The arrests were carried out by FIA under the federal state; direct Sharif ordering is not established, but the pattern persisted under his government.","contrary_evidence":["The source does not prove Sharif personally ordered the arrests."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.6","4B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan: Braving the Storm: Enforced disappearances and the right to protest in Pakistan","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-08-11","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/documents/asa33/5872/2022/en/","claim":"Families of the disappeared and activists who protest peacefully are sometimes met with violence by the state, intimidation, and arbitrary detention or arrest for exercising peaceful assembly.","locator":"line 66","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Detailed campaign digest with direct rights-violation findings and date-specific framing; strong on the existence of the abuse pattern.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 reporting on protest and disappearance-related abuse.","ruler_attribution":"This is state-level attribution rather than a single Sharif order; it captures the domestic safety climate under his government but much of the problem predates him.","contrary_evidence":["Some of the underlying disappearance problem predates Sharif and is not uniquely attributable to him."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.8","4B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan police fire teargas, baton-charge, round up supporters of ousted PM Khan","publisher":"The Business Standard / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-05-25","url":"https://www.tbsnews.net/world/south-asia/pakistan-police-fire-teargas-baton-charge-round-supporters-ousted-pm-khan-426638","claim":"Pakistani police fired teargas, baton-charged, and detained supporters of ousted PM Imran Khan to stop them reaching Islamabad to demand fresh elections.","locator":"lines 161-164","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting with concrete incident details and witnesses; attribution to national-level command is indirect, but the protest suppression itself is well documented.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct May 2022 protest suppression inside the target year.","ruler_attribution":"The action was carried out by police and other authorities during the Sharif era; direct PM ordering is not shown, so attribution is institutional rather than personal.","contrary_evidence":["Authorities justified the response as keeping order around an unannounced road blockade.","Direct Sharif instruction is not established in the report."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.8","4B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Behind Pakistan’s civilian government, army tightens its grip on journalists","publisher":"RSF","publication_date":"2022-07-13","url":"https://rsf.org/en/behind-pakistan-s-civilian-government-army-tightens-its-grip-journalists","claim":"RSF said it had registered nine cases of intimidation of Pakistani journalists by army-related agencies since Shehbaz Sharif became prime minister and warned the harassment was undermining democracy.","locator":"lines 328-330 and 352-360","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Dated advocacy report with named cases and explicit attribution; strong on the pattern, though the military-centric attribution limits direct PM culpability.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Mid-2022, squarely within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"RSF links the harassment mainly to army-related agencies, which limits direct attribution to Sharif but still places the pattern under his watch.","contrary_evidence":["RSF itself says the military was acting behind the scenes, so this is not a clean civilian-only responsibility case."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.6","4B.9","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistani TV news channel taken off the air, news director arrested","publisher":"RSF","publication_date":"2022-08-11","url":"https://rsf.org/en/pakistani-tv-news-channel-taken-air-news-director-arrested","claim":"ARY News was taken off the air in most major Pakistani cities and its news director was arrested; RSF said the civilian government was responsible for the latest attacks on the media while the military intervened behind the scenes.","locator":"lines 315-338","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Specific dated incident with direct reporting and explicit attribution commentary, though the source itself notes behind-the-scenes military involvement.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"August 2022 action in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"The report holds the current civilian government responsible for the latest attack while also pointing to military influence, so attribution is shared and incomplete rather than purely personal to Sharif.","contrary_evidence":["The source says the military high command stamped the censorship, limiting direct attribution to the civilian prime minister.","The same report emphasizes recurring pressure across alternating governments."],"lenses":["4B.6","4B.9","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan: Rights Besieged Amid Political Turmoil","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2023-01-12","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/01/12/pakistan-rights-besieged-amid-political-turmoil","claim":"HRW said Pakistani authorities harassed and prosecuted human rights defenders and journalists for criticizing government policies, used blasphemy accusations and sedition laws against opponents and journalists, and failed to protect minorities and other at-risk groups in 2022.","locator":"lines 608-615","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"A retrospective annual report with concrete 2022 incidents and multiple corroborating themes; strong synthesis though it attributes broadly to authorities rather than a single decision-maker.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective but directly about 2022 conduct under the Sharif government.","ruler_attribution":"Attribution is to Pakistani authorities during 2022, including the Sharif government, but the report does not isolate direct prime-ministerial commands.","contrary_evidence":["This is a broad retrospective and not proof of a single Sharif order for each incident.","Some abuses predate Sharif and are institutional rather than personal."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.6","4B.7","4B.9","4B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
- I reviewed about 30 documents across official records, courts, rights groups, local and international media, and a few local-language sources.
- I kept 11 new source-claim units and one reused transfer-of-power item, with one Urdu source retained for local-language coverage and one official state-media item retained for direct government actions.
- I rejected duplicate syndications of the same April transfer story, redundant reposts of the same media-crackdown episodes, and out-of-period pieces that only repeated inherited baseline conditions.
- I dropped some potentially relevant but duplicative items, including a February PECA/NCHR critique that mostly described inherited pre-Sharif context, and other media-freedom stories that did not add a distinct 2022 claim beyond the stronger items already kept.
- I excluded flood, economic, and foreign-policy articles because they did not materially answer Chapter 4B, and I excluded claims where responsibility sat mainly with provincial or military actors unless the source also tied them to the federal government.

**Remaining gaps**
- Direct evidence that Sharif personally ordered specific arrests, censorship moves, or protest crackdowns is still thin; many events are better attributed to FIA, PEMRA, police, or army-linked agencies.
- 4B.2 and 4B.5 remain comparatively weak: I found more on media/protest pressure than on electoral-rule manipulation or personality-cult style institutional capture.
- More search would help on cabinet-level or parliamentary records, Urdu-language reporting on PECA/PEMRA implementation, and any formal investigations into journalist harassment or protest policing.
